# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and this package divide the work rather than overlap, along a single line:\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) et ce paquet se partagent le travail au lieu de se chevaucher, selon une seule ligne de partage :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| ffsim owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | `qiskit-fermions` owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| The high-level ansatz *operators* ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") and their siblings), built from coupled-cluster amplitudes or a parameter vector | The fermionic *circuit* ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")) those operators become, and its transpilation into a qubit circuit under any fermion-to-qubit encoding |\n"
"| Fast simulation in a compact fixed-particle-number space                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | The mapper framework and the operator data structures the circuit is built from                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
msgstr ""
"| ffsim s'occupe de | `qiskit-fermions` s'occupe de |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| Les *opérateurs* d'ansatz de haut niveau ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") et leurs variantes), construits à partir d'amplitudes de cluster couplé ou d'un vecteur de paramètres | Le *circuit* fermionique ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")) en lequel ces opérateurs se transforment, et sa transpilation en circuit de qubits sous n'importe quel encodage fermion-vers-qubit |\n"
"| La simulation rapide dans un espace compact à nombre de particules fixe | Le framework de mappers et les structures de données d'opérateurs à partir desquelles le circuit est construit |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The practical consequence runs both ways. The ansatz math lives in ffsim, so [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") and [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") take an ffsim operator directly as their input. Conversely, ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, so lowering one of its ansatz operators through a *different* encoding is what bringing it here buys you.\n"
msgstr "La conséquence pratique va dans les deux sens. Les mathématiques de l'ansatz résident dans ffsim, donc [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") et [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") prennent directement un opérateur ffsim en entrée. À l'inverse, les portes Qiskit propres à ffsim sont spécifiques à la transformation de Jordan-Wigner, donc ce que t'apporte leur utilisation ici, c'est de pouvoir abaisser l'un de ses opérateurs d'ansatz via un encodage *différent*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulation is where the two meet, and this guide explains how. ffsim is this package’s simulation backend, reached through its own protocols rather than a wrapper: the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) calls [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\"), and [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") directly on [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")objects and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")objects, with no conversion step.\n"
msgstr "La simulation est le point de rencontre des deux, et ce guide explique comment. ffsim est le backend de simulation de ce paquet, atteint par ses propres protocoles plutôt que par une enveloppe : le [guide SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) appelle [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") et [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") directement sur des objets [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") et [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), sans étape de conversion.\n"

